WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.223
JavaScript input validation requires explicit runtime checks.

00:00:03.223 --> 00:00:07.239
Browser controls, TypeScript types, and framework conventions are helpful,

00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:10.362
but they are not enough by themselves.

00:00:10.362 --> 00:00:15.270
Values from users, browsers, APIs, files, storage, messages, queues, third-party services,

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:22.409
and environment variables should be treated as untrusted until the application has parsed and validated them.

00:00:22.409 --> 00:00:25.086
Strong validation starts with expected data.

00:00:25.086 --> 00:00:29.994
Define type, length, format, range, required fields, optional fields, allowed values,

00:00:29.994 --> 00:00:34.010
nested objects, arrays, and business rules before processing data.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:37.580
Be careful with dynamic typing and type coercion.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:42.488
Prefer clear checks and schemas over loose comparisons and ambiguous assumptions.

00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:45.611
Schema libraries can make validation more consistent.

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:47.396
Zod, Joi, Yup, Ajv,

00:00:47.396 --> 00:00:52.304
and JSON Schema can define contracts and enforce them at runtime,

00:00:52.304 --> 00:00:54.088
especially at API boundaries.

00:00:54.088 --> 00:00:56.319
Client-side validation improves user experience,

00:00:56.319 --> 00:00:59.443
but server-side validation is the security requirement.

00:00:59.443 --> 00:01:05.243
Shared schemas can help reduce drift, but the server remains responsible for enforcement.

00:01:05.243 --> 00:01:09.259
The goal is predictable behavior and reduced security risk.

00:01:09.259 --> 00:01:14.167
Validate by context, pair validation with output encoding and safe APIs,

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:19.075
reject fields users should not control, and test failure cases thoroughly.

00:01:19.075 --> 00:01:23.983
JavaScript applications are safer when invalid input is expected, handled deliberately,

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:26.660
and prevented from reaching sensitive logic.
